1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,332
Rivers carry contamination downstream faster than any lab result comes back.

2
00:00:05,332 --> 00:00:08,639
PathoStream EHR detects it, forecasts where it goes,

3
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:11,691
and warns the doctor before the patients arrive,

4
00:00:11,691 --> 00:00:14,934
using the open health standards FHIR and CDS Hooks.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,092
This is the water-authority dashboard.

6
00:00:18,092 --> 00:00:22,129
Nine real European rivers, forty-one monitoring stations,

7
00:00:22,129 --> 00:00:26,025
fifteen EU countries, and one pipeline for every river:

8
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:27,725
detect, forecast, alert.

9
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,512
On German reaches, this live badge is real water-level data from

10
00:00:32,512 --> 00:00:36,265
PEGELONLINE, kept visibly separate from our simulated detector.

11
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,151
Detection path one.

12
00:00:38,151 --> 00:00:44,174
A water-authority operator confirms contamination at Ponte de Santa Clara, in Coimbra.

13
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,044
Instantly, a transport model forecasts when the plume reaches each downstream

14
00:00:51,044 --> 00:00:55,174
station, with a ninety percent travel-time band instead of one falsely

15
00:00:55,174 --> 00:00:56,059
precise number.

16
00:00:56,059 --> 00:00:58,479
We move the clock forward twenty minutes.

17
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:01,347
Now the doctor’s screen.

18
00:01:01,347 --> 00:01:04,846
A patient living on the affected reach gets a CDS Hooks

19
00:01:04,846 --> 00:01:07,518
card inside their health record: critical,

20
00:01:07,518 --> 00:01:10,827
an active exposure window, and a concrete next step,

21
00:01:10,827 --> 00:01:14,390
a stool pathogen PCR panel with its verified LOINC code.

22
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:17,899
Path two: nobody reports anything.

23
00:01:17,899 --> 00:01:20,285
We inject a rising turbidity trend.

24
00:01:20,285 --> 00:01:24,991
An EWMA control chart, the method used in industrial quality control,

25
00:01:24,991 --> 00:01:30,514
watches for sustained drift, and after six consecutive out-of-control readings it

26
00:01:30,514 --> 00:01:31,946
escalates on its own.

27
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,730
Same patient, weaker evidence, different card.

28
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:43,359
A statistical signal is not a lab result,

29
00:01:43,359 --> 00:01:46,116
so this is a warning, labelled unconfirmed,

30
00:01:46,116 --> 00:01:48,617
with no instruction to start treatment.

31
00:01:48,617 --> 00:01:52,080
The alert always matches the strength of the evidence.

32
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:56,385
Path three: a member of the public reports cloudy water,

33
00:01:56,385 --> 00:01:58,424
a strange odour and dead fish.

34
00:01:58,424 --> 00:02:03,249
A trained classifier triages the report and shows exactly which answers

35
00:02:03,249 --> 00:02:04,336
drove its score.

36
00:02:04,336 --> 00:02:05,220
No black box.

37
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,301
But the AI never confirms anything.

38
00:02:17,301 --> 00:02:20,571
Only a water-authority reviewer can promote the report.

39
00:02:20,571 --> 00:02:22,949
Then the doctor’s card is full strength,

40
00:02:22,949 --> 00:02:26,754
and says honestly that the source was a reviewed citizen report.

41
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:33,028
Every confirmation, escalation and forecast lands on one incident timeline,

42
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:35,320
the audit trail across all nine rivers.

43
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:36,896
Now the AI layer.

44
00:02:36,896 --> 00:02:39,365
Four agents: a Sentinel for river data,

45
00:02:39,365 --> 00:02:43,606
Citizen Intel, Clinical Triage, and a Commander that combines them.

46
00:02:43,606 --> 00:02:47,974
Google Gemini drives the investigation, choosing which tools to call,

47
00:02:47,974 --> 00:02:50,886
while a safety guard checks every single call.

48
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:57,100
The evidence is human-confirmed, so the Commander proposes a recreational closure,

49
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,330
but only as a draft.

50
00:02:58,330 --> 00:03:00,666
The banner counts Gemini’s tool calls,

51
00:03:00,666 --> 00:03:03,063
and shows clinical triage stayed local,

52
00:03:03,063 --> 00:03:06,444
because patient data is not sent to a model by default.

53
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:11,213
These summaries are written by Gemini and clearly labelled.

54
00:03:11,213 --> 00:03:14,947
They describe the evidence, but cannot change a single number,

55
00:03:14,947 --> 00:03:16,211
severity or proposal.

56
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:21,628
The municipal and clinician notices are drafts, with FHIR status preparation.

57
00:03:21,628 --> 00:03:23,744
A human authority must approve them.

58
00:03:23,744 --> 00:03:25,920
Nothing is ever issued automatically.

59
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:30,055
And every step is traceable: which tools Gemini requested,

60
00:03:30,055 --> 00:03:33,877
which ran deterministically, and any call the guard rejected,

61
00:03:33,877 --> 00:03:34,880
with the reason.

62
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,495
Now the contrast.

63
00:03:36,495 --> 00:03:41,086
We cleared the confirmed flags and left only this statistical anomaly,

64
00:03:41,086 --> 00:03:42,856
with no human confirmation.

65
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,288
We run the same agents again,

66
00:03:45,288 --> 00:03:47,408
for a patient with bloody diarrhoea,

67
00:03:47,408 --> 00:03:50,176
and Gemini investigates through the same guard.

68
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:56,323
With only an unconfirmed signal, the one thing the system may

69
00:03:56,323 --> 00:03:58,614
propose is confirmatory water sampling.

70
00:03:58,614 --> 00:04:02,960
Never a boil-water advisory, even though a reviewed citizen report agrees.

71
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:07,459
Clinically, pathogen scores are labelled heuristics, not probabilities.

72
00:04:07,459 --> 00:04:09,430
The Shiga-toxin test shows no code,

73
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:12,021
because only verified LOINC codes are emitted.

74
00:04:12,021 --> 00:04:15,400
And review priority stays routine for an unconfirmed signal.

75
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:19,425
Nothing is guessed: bad coordinates are refused.

76
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:23,583
The Gemini safeguards: a tool allowlist per agent,

77
00:04:23,583 --> 00:04:27,747
scope locked to the request, patient details bound on the server,

78
00:04:27,747 --> 00:04:29,669
and a call budget and timeout.

79
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:33,256
Whatever the model does, the assessment stays identical.

80
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:38,244
PathoStream EHR: warn the doctor before the patients arrive.

81
00:04:38,244 --> 00:04:40,808
A research prototype on synthetic data,

82
00:04:40,808 --> 00:04:45,212
not a medical device, backed by a fourteen-hazard safety case where

83
00:04:45,212 --> 00:04:48,367
every implemented control has an automated test.

84
00:04:48,367 --> 00:04:49,025
Thank you.

